{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('task/task_contract.json'));m=json.loads(p['method']['description']);\nfor k,v in m.items():print(k,':',v,'\\\\n')\nprint('TOP',list(p))\nq=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'));print('REF SHAPE',list(q),q['references'][0]);\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"aggregation : Within episode equal mean of three nonzero edit budgets (1/3 each); equal seeds within case (1/3 production, identity smoke); Arena single crowd case identity; NBA equal seasons (1/3 search,1/5 final); equal family weights1/2,1/2. Each Arena seed weight1/6, each NBA search seed-case1/18, final1/30 before budget. Random baselines average streams first (4 search,8 final,1 smoke). All failed/missing episodes retain zero score/baseline/displacement and influence_error=control_error=1, validity/correct=0 at original weights. Method-audit failure retains zero candidate score/displacement and influence_error1. Flags are conjunctions, not means. No survivor renormalization. \n\naudits : Independent trusted Newton fitting max100 iterations, max35 line-search backtracks, gradient infinity norm <2e-7; ridge1; candidate scores/audit derivatives/directional influences/prefix shift arithmetic allclose atol2e-5 rtol2e-4 (scores) or3e-3 (derivatives). Eight deterministic evenly spaced audit rows; finite difference epsilon1e-3, derivative allclose atol2e-5 rtol3e-3. This verifies executable influence arithmetic and independent fit/selection outputs, not hidden candidate internals. Nonlinear exact-refit prediction discrepancy norm/(1+norm) is reported as influence_error, not a superiority or linear-accuracy threshold. \n\nbaselines : Uniform random eligible flips; degree-sum quartile-stratified random flips matching each prefix of ACTUAL candidate selected row degree bins (approximate exposure matching, not exact endpoint matching); smallest absolute fitted matchup margin heuristic. Equal edit budgets, observed inputs and fixed random streams; baselines receive no candidate-only feedback. Streams seeded episode_seed+8371; actual degree matching seed+72831; grouped bootstrap seed+49207. Candidate may select alternative nested feasible sets; numerical directional influence/audit calculations and predicted prefix shifts must remain genuine. \n\ncontrols : Canonical controls declared before scoring: (1) evaluator copy/no-op refit identical scores atol1e-9; (2) evaluator constant-zero predictor must be rejected by known nonzero exact-refit shift >.01 on explicitly synthetic 3-game 2-participant diagnostic, never substituted for real-data evidence; (3) rotate eligible directional priorities by one, require nonidentity priorities, different selected row set AND nonidentical refitted coefficients atol1e-9; matched budgets, no superiority gate; vacuity retains failed/inconclusive control; (4) immediately after required reset, analyze token input without data returns exactly error:no_data so previously legal state cannot be reused. Four control types weight1/4 each, each has one conjunction assertion. No controls expose labels, metrics or reference results via candidate RPC. \n\ndeadlines : One invocation deadline starts before loading, subtract conservative startup allowance120s search/300s final, reserve finish60s/120s. All episode resets globally reserve2s plus8s worst-case overhead each, including sequential candidate+worker termination/reap/stderr teardown. Each production episode reserves reference four methods30s each, candidate30s, scoring/controls/uncertainty90s search (=240 productive allowance); final90s each reference/candidate and210s scoring (=660). Ref methods have individual work alarms; parent reference worker total122/362 bounds, with explicit3s dispatch slack. Same candidate30/90 allowance per method, fixed estimator and edits. Each remaining reset reservation is retained on timeout. No canonical minimum productive baseline time exists. Actual productive reference work is measured excluding startup/imports/reset/output. Reduced smoke120s total subtracts2s startup,3s finish, reset2s+overhead2s each, reference individual1s/total5s, candidate1s, scoring4s with1 replicate; same cases/order/operations/loading/imports/isolation. Smoke does not attest production feasibility. \n\nfinal_correct : Separately require all final cases/seeds/transcript and the same operational/scientific validity checks on sealed data. No comparative-superiority requirement. Final claim assessment uses paired effects/uncertainty and manuscript review; unsubstantiated superiority claims must be removed, not retroactively made search vetoes. Paper novelty/acceptance is NOT automated by numeric correct. \n\nlimitations : Operational proxy does not itself write/review the required conference PDF/LaTeX/checklist, assess novelty, inspect forbidden literature, prove opaque hidden mechanisms or establish causality across unequal comparison graphs. Publication requires human/scientific evidence review of actual manuscript and reproducibility artifacts. No held-out predictive-target task, adaptation requirement or learning/state-hash gate is invented. Methods optimize feasible observed-outcome perturbations, not historical misconduct. Fixed regularization, fractional ties, graph coverage, coarse degree matching and fixed intervention plans in bootstrap bound interpretation. Final data/outcomes cannot be used for search tuning. \n\noperational : Linux x86-64 CPython3.11-3.13 (draft tested3.12), libseccomp.so.2, Landlock ABI>=3 for native validation; no GPU. 4 CPU cores/8GiB aggregate, at most2 active compute cores/threads and4GiB per role. Explicit thread environment, native/trusted subprocess address-space limits and all-thread CPU ceiling ceil(2*plane_wall), killable monotonic wall transport. Harness owns isolated production quotas. Native candidate has clean allowlisted environment, private copied single-file source and Landlock filesystem/seccomp network isolation; no evaluator resources/results/credentials mount. Only fixed proxy path plus socket authenticates in-process broker loading; proxy calls use bounded alarm, never child-launched. Final standalone requires own file, own resources and installed dependencies/harness only. \n\noperations_per_episode : {'analyze': 1, 'download_chunk_max': 16, 'reset': 1, 'reset_probe_analyze_no_data': 1, 'upload_chunk_max': 16, 'upload_commit': 1, 'upload_start': 1} \n\nrpc_derivation : 37 per episode using declared maximum 16 input and 16 output chunks, including setup/commit even for one chunk. Search 4 cases x3 seeds x37=444. Final 6 cases x3 seeds x37=666. No replay, retries, export/import state transfer, extra training or diagnostic resets. Evaluator-only copy/constant/permutation/refit/bootstrap operations use zero broker calls; reset control is the counted probe. Mock maximum transcript and scheduler/failure tests precede production. \n\nscientific_workload : Arena: all 14272 search and 43205 final usable comparisons; NBA all unique games in 2006-2008 search and 2011-2015 final, season-specific participant universes. No Elo inputs. Sum logistic loss plus 0.5*L2 norm squared, ridge=1 for participant and optional home coefficients, centered participant scores; ties y=.5 included in fitting but cannot be edited. Fractions .001,.005,.01 of ALL usable rows, floor to integer, binary outcome flips, distinct nested prefix sets. A zero positive-budget edit count is invalid. Deterministic tie order is participant index in lexicographically sorted source names. \n\nsearch_correct : Complete planned search reset transcript; valid bounded protocol and content-provenance integrity; feasible actual nested row edits; genuine numerically audited influence arithmetic; successful converged independent fits, required baselines and all nonvacuous controls; complete finite fixed-weight evidence; no isolation/leakage/resource violation. No large-sensitivity or baseline-superiority threshold. scientific_valid records mandatory estimator/method/control completeness; correct additionally requires operational/integrity completion. Eligible candidates ranked descending combined_score. A schema-valid state_changed or other self-report never contributes evidence. \n\nuncertainty : Arena raw-document connected components and NBA unique games are grouped bootstrap units within each fixed panel, 10 search and30 final replicates per case/seed (1 smoke). Bootstrap original and fixed candidate/baseline nested interventions paired under identical group multiplicity weights; all random streams participate. Report 2.5/97.5 percentile rank intervals and paired candidate-minus-baseline effects. Failed required refits/resamples preserve entire episode worst-case evidence rather than intervals over survivors. Three seeds are algorithmic variation, not independent datasets. Sports conclusions are descriptive of fixed seasons, not causal effects of design. \n\nwire : Only finite inline JSON lines, no paths or shared files. little-endian float64 observed [n,4] a,b,y,z, maximum input/output decoded size 16MiB each in candidate RAM, chunk 1MiB max, maximum 16 chunks each direction; participant cap256, n cap524288. Every actual line plus representative request_id/payload/error envelope and LF framing is serialized and checked <8MiB locally and strictly <64MiB harness limit. Full-sized representative base64 chunks preflight at 1398185 bytes or less including line metadata; larger framing has more than 56MiB unused harness headroom. \n\nTOP ['schema_version', 'canonical_task', 'method', 'candidate', 'evaluators', 'resources', 'data', 'metrics', 'upstream', 'provenance', 'compute', 'protocol', 'feedback', 'publication']\nREF SHAPE ['campaign_results_dir', 'count', 'generated_at', 'queries', 'reference_query_plan', 'references', 'results_dir'] {'citation_count': 4026, 'citation_key': 'Koh2017UnderstandingBP', 'id': 'ref.s2.08ad8fad21f6ec4cda4d56be1