{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_144","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: retrieve_permitted.py\n@@\n-    ('Ford1957', '10.2307/2308513'),\n+    ('Maystre2015', 'openalex:W1948584817'),\n@@\n-        url = f'https://api.openalex.org/works/https://doi.org/{identifier}'\n+        url = f'https://api.openalex.org/works/{identifier.split(\\\":\\\", 1)[1]}' if identifier.startswith('openalex:') else f'https://api.openalex.org/works/https://doi.org/{identifier}'\n@@\n-        crossref = requests.get(f'https://api.crossref.org/works/{identifier}', timeout=45)\n-        cross = crossref.json()['message'] if crossref.ok else {\n+        crossref = None if identifier.startswith('openalex:') else requests.get(f'https://api.crossref.org/works/{identifier}', timeout=45)\n+        cross = crossref.json()['message'] if crossref is not None and crossref.ok else {\n@@\n-        bib = f'@{entry_type}{{{key},\\\\n title={{{title}}},\\\\n author={{{\\\" and \\\".join(authors)}}},\\\\n year={{{year}}},\\\\n {\\\"publisher\\\" if entry_type == \\\"book\\\" else \\\"journal\\\"}={{{cross.get(\\\"publisher\\\", \\\"\\\") if entry_type == \\\"book\\\" else venue}}},\\\\n doi={{{identifier}}}'\n+        bib = f'@{entry_type}{{{key},\\\\n title={{{title}}},\\\\n author={{{\\\" and \\\".join(authors)}}},\\\\n year={{{year}}},\\\\n {\\\"publisher\\\" if entry_type == \\\"book\\\" else \\\"journal\\\"}={{{cross.get(\\\"publisher\\\", \\\"\\\") if entry_type == \\\"book\\\" else venue}}},\\\\n {\\\"url\\\" if identifier.startswith(\\\"openalex:\\\") else \\\"doi\\\"}={{{url if identifier.startswith(\\\"openalex:\\\") else identifier}}}'\n*** Update File: paper.tex\n@@\n-Statistical comparison models connect qualitative judgments to latent scales \\\\citep{Thurstone1927}; tournament-strength estimation also has a long likelihood-based history \\\\citep{Zermelo1929,Ford1957}. Bradley--Terry fitting and its generalizations have established computational treatments \\\\citep{Hunter2004,Turner2012}. Explicit tie models introduce additional structure \\\\citep{Rao1967,Davidson1970}; our fractional-outcome convention instead preserves the fixed estimator under study. These are different modeling choices, not interchangeable implementations. Separation can complicate unpenalized logistic estimation \\\\citep{Albert1984}; our fixed quadratic penalty is also distinct from bias-reduced likelihood estimation \\\\citep{Firth1993}.\n+Statistical comparison models connect qualitative judgments to latent scales \\\\citep{Thurstone1927}; tournament-strength estimation also has a long likelihood-based history \\\\citep{Zermelo1929}. Bradley--Terry fitting and its generalizations have established computational treatments \\\\citep{Hunter2004,Turner2012}; spectral inference offers another computational perspective on choice models \\\\citep{Maystre2015}. Explicit tie models introduce additional structure \\\\citep{Rao1967,Davidson1970}; our fractional-outcome convention instead preserves the fixed estimator under study. Separation can complicate unpenalized logistic estimation \\\\citep{Albert1984}; our fixed quadratic penalty is distinct from bias-reduced likelihood estimation \\\\citep{Firth1993}.\n@@\n-Guided disruption is larger than each control's seed-averaged point estimate in every plotted case--budget cell. The family-balanced budget-average is \"'$0.05564$ for guided refitting, versus $0.00935$ for uniform changes, $0.01115$ for degree-stratified changes, and $0.00757$ for the small-margin heuristic. The secondary normalized mean rank displacement is $0.04409$. These aggregate quantities have different meanings; neither should be relabeled as predictive accuracy or as a percentage of incorrect leaderboard entries.\n+Guided budget-averaged disruption exceeds each control'\"'s seed-averaged point estimate on every panel. At individual budgets, NBA 2014's smallest guided intervention ties the small-margin control; the other plotted cells favor guidance. The family-balanced budget-average is \"'$0.05564$ for guided refitting, versus $0.00935$ for uniform changes, $0.01115$ for degree-stratified changes, and $0.00757$ for the small-margin heuristic. The secondary normalized mean rank displacement is $0.04409$. These are not predictive accuracies or percentages of incorrect leaderboard entries.\n@@\n-'\"\\\\paragraph{Reproducibility and evidence boundaries.}\n-The supplement identifies inspectable preparation and selection sources, records the observed seed summaries, and separates arithmetic replay of supplied results from fresh evaluation. Numerical checks support the recorded estimator and intervention calculations; they do not certify every internal search operation, global optimality, or substantive novelty. The current paper introduces no new evaluations or unrecorded ablations. The concept overview is explanatory only; all plotted measurements are replayed from the final evidence arrays. This distinction prevents a readable schematic or an accepted protocol check from becoming unsupported empirical evidence.\n+\\\\paragraph{Evidence boundaries.}\n+The supplement supplies inspectable sources and individual seed summaries. Numerical checks do not certify every internal search operation, global optimality, or novelty. All plotted measurements are replayed from final evidence; no new evaluation or component ablation is introduced.\n*** Update File: build_claims.py\n@@\n-add('Guided seed-averaged disruption exceeds each comparator in every case-budget cell; this does not imply universally positive paired uncertainty.',\n+add('Guided budget-averaged disruption exceeds each comparator on every panel. At the smallest NBA 2014 budget, guidance ties the small-margin control; the other plotted seed-averaged cells favor guidance. This does not imply universally positive paired uncertainty.',\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython retrieve_permitted.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
