{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_159","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/tmp/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: build_figures.py\n@@\n import json\n+import re\n@@\n EPISODES = DATA['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']\n # @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n+PROTOCOL = json.loads(json.loads((ROOT / 'source_evidence/task_contract.json').read_text())['method']['description'])\n+NOMINAL = [float(value) for value in re.search(r'Fractions ([.0-9,]+) of', PROTOCOL['scientific_workload']).group(1).split(',')]\n+# @evidence[[source_evidence/task_contract.json#/method]]\n@@\n-    axis.set_title(f'({chr(97 + budget)}) Nominal edits: {[\\\"0.1%\\\", \\\"0.5%\\\", \\\"1.0%\\\"][budget]}', loc='left', pad=2)\n+    axis.set_title(f'({chr(97 + budget)}) Nominal edits: {100 * NOMINAL[budget]:.1f}%', loc='left', pad=2)\n@@\n-        'min_font_size_pt': 9 if concept else 8, 'max_panels_per_row': 2 if concept else 1,\n+        'min_font_size_pt': 9 if concept else 8, 'panels_per_row': 2 if concept else 1,\n*** Add File: literature/reading_scope.md\n+# Reading and access scope\n+\n+References are selected by their relevance to the fixed-estimator study, not to fill a generic optimization bibliography. Direct identified works and bounded older-method queries were used; no citation expansion or broad ranking-attack search was used.\n+\n+Original abstract text was consulted for all cited sources except Zermelo (1929), whose original scanned article was retrieved from Springer and the opening model/likelihood pages inspected. For Koh, Broderick, Chiang, Jiang, and Negahban, original PDFs were also retrieved and abstract/introduction excerpts inspected. For Bubeck, the original abstract and contents were inspected. These are not claims of cover-to-cover reading. Remaining citations are limited to the general subject or method explicitly described in the original abstract text retained through OpenAlex/Crossref or the original arXiv abstract page. No theorem, numerical result, or novelty comparison is attributed to an uninspected section.\n+\n+Bradley–Terry's original article was not retained as a citation because the available metadata lacked an abstract and attempted direct original-source access returned access errors. Hunter's consulted methodological abstract supports the model attribution instead. Ford's original record supplied a bibliographic string rather than substantive abstract text; it was not cited. Inaccessible or unsuitable records (including White, Kendall and an introductory bootstrap book) were replaced by relevant originals with readable abstract text. Unrelated automated retrievals were not cited.\n+\n+Exact identifier lookup initially failed for one ranking-list DOI and one Huber proceedings DOI. The ranking-list DOI was corrected by a bounded pre-2009 exact-title Crossref lookup; the unavailable Huber proceedings entry was replaced by Huber's original robust-location article. An initially guessed arXiv identifier resolved to the unrelated 2015 article *SEISMIC: A Self-Exciting Point Process Model for Predicting Tweet Popularity*. Only its title metadata was inspected; it was not cited or used. Maystre and Grossglauser's identified older work was instead retrieved by a bounded pre-2017 exact-title OpenAlex query.\n+\n+No known prohibited study, mirror, discussion, or citation-expansion page was encountered. Nothing was inferred about its identity. Failed endpoints and unrelated title-only records do not support manuscript claims. Bibliographic identifiers, retrieved abstract text, available original PDFs, and reading scope are retained for auditing. No literature-derived numeric result is presented as a measurement of this study.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n/tmp/paper-venv/bin/python build_figures.py\npython build_claims.py\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=json.load(open('references_provenance.json'))\nfor r in p['references']:\n key=r['citation_key'];r['reading_notes_path']='literature/reading_scope.md'\n if key=='Zermelo1929':r['reading_scope']='Original scanned article, opening model and likelihood pages inspected';r['original_pdf_path']='literature/Zermelo1929.pdf'\n elif key in ['Koh2017','Broderick2020','Chiang2024','Jiang2011','Negahban2017']:r['reading_scope']='Original abstract and original PDF abstract/introduction excerpts inspected';r['original_pdf_path']=f'literature/{key}.pdf'\n elif key=='Bubeck2015':r['reading_scope']='Original abstract and PDF contents inspected';r['original_pdf_path']='literature/Bubeck2015.pdf'\n else:r['reading_scope']='Original abstract text consulted; not a full-text reading claim'\nPath('references_provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
